Z||000000||Philphine||06-13-2001||08:19 PM||||is there any difference bettween them from year to year. i may try one off an '84 4sp. on my '87 5 sp. i hate k-balling but my chop top is so much in the project stage that i won't feel too bad about it (plus i don't want to pay for a new one right now).<P>i've been having problems shifting my '87 after i gone a few miles. even stanger, i'll sometimes get easy shifts a few times then it gets hard again. i decided to try and bleed the system today but each time i tried it i lost more and more clutch action. the only thing i can find from looking is some seepage around the mc rod inside the car. <P>the clutch, mc and slave cylinder were all changed about 2 years ago and i'm hoping i don't need another clutch. i still have the old slave cyl. (good. changed it before finding out i needed a clutch), but i don't think it's my problem anyway. <P>finding out i need a new clutch again is going to dampen the old fiero spirit. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||06-13-2001||09:29 PM||||The master cylinder from the '84 won't work on the '87.<P>When you replaced then 2 year ago, were they original GM parts or aftermarket?  If it's the latter, then you may need to replace them again.....the aftermarket parts don't seem to last long at all.||||reg||1
